# HL-LN-DIAG2 (SOFT, OWNER-SKIPPED by default, also a block separator: un-skip it with SKIP when HL-LN-DIAG reproduced the failure and the clock allows a second fresh boot; the repeat of HL-LN-DIAG, the diagnosis of s0808b's HL-LN failure): the same Lever N hang-shape smoke that failed there (SMOKE_CHECK: 'two prefill steps of <req> ran back to back with N decoder(s) running: the alternation did not
# yield', run 37773733305, v584), on the same TRAFFIC profile and the same image, a FRESH boot, with the debug logs the code offers turned on through C2_SMOKE_ENV (c2_serving_job.py SMOKE_ENV_ALLOWED, docker run -e):
#   QWEN_FAST_SEQ_STAGE_LOG=1  (trace_census.py STAGE_LOG_FLAG: a flushed '[SEQ-STAGE]' begin line before each packed stage, so the steps around a back-to-back pair show what ran between them)
#   VLLM_LOGGING_LEVEL=DEBUG   (the vLLM scheduler and engine-core DEBUG lines beside the plugin scheduler's own '[PINDIAG] lever N step/park/short lane/prefill gate' lines, which are on in every Lever N boot)
#   QWEN_PREFIX_STATS_S=5      (qwen_prefix_scheduler_patch.py: the '[PINDIAG] prefix: stats' line every 5 s instead of the default, so the registry state is on the timeline of the failing pair)
# QWEN_FAST_PHASE_LOG=1 is already on in the image (docker/qwen-c2-serving.Dockerfile:138), and the profile's QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_* flags are not touched: NO digest, NO audit, NO fault, NO census graph. The profile is the traffic profile unchanged.
# READ (a FAILURE of this job is the expected finding, not a stop): save container.log and smoke.log; for each 'did not yield' pair read, between the two steps, the decode steps (kind=decode seats>=1), the 'reason=' and 'owed_ms/owed_rounds' of the
# second step, the park/short-lane lines and the DEBUG scheduler lines. s0808b's v584 pairs had reason=paid owed_ms=0 owed_rounds=0 f_eff=1.000 with seats=1..3 and no decode step between them.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the third session of 2026-10-08/09 (s0809). ORDER.txt has the order, the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the Lever N traffic profile
# baked in as its default). C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box: the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run. NO profile of this pack carries a digest or an audit (QWEN_PREFIX_DIGESTS, QWEN_PREFIX_AUDIT, the lever audits): test_tp4_session_0809 pins that.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,levern_decoder_finishes,levern_all_decoders_finish,levern_cancel_mid_prefill,levern_arrival_during_prefill,levern_seed_stops,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_drain,concurrent8_skew
C2_SMOKE_ENV=QWEN_FAST_SEQ_STAGE_LOG=1 VLLM_LOGGING_LEVEL=DEBUG QWEN_PREFIX_STATS_S=5
C2_BOX_MINUTES=45
